WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.510
Our data lands in Apache Iceberg tables,

2
00:00:02.820 --> 00:00:05.530
Parquet files plus metadata in object storage,

3
00:00:05.840 --> 00:00:07.410
so any engine can read them.

4
00:00:08.020 --> 00:00:10.620
Apache Polaris is the Iceberg catalog, it

5
00:00:10.640 --> 00:00:12.580
knows where each table's files are and

6
00:00:12.600 --> 00:00:13.950
decides who may read them.

7
00:00:14.500 --> 00:00:17.180
ClickHouse queries those tables directly, it asks

8
00:00:17.200 --> 00:00:19.220
Polaris to load the table, then reads

9
00:00:19.240 --> 00:00:21.580
the manifests and Parquet files from storage

10
00:00:21.600 --> 00:00:22.270
itself.

11
00:00:23.000 --> 00:00:25.530
Reading those files needs a storage credential,

12
00:00:25.940 --> 00:00:28.060
either ClickHouse brings its own key, or

13
00:00:28.080 --> 00:00:29.880
Polaris vends one, short-lived.

14
00:00:29.900 --> 00:00:32.280
And scoped to that table's files, that's

15
00:00:32.300 --> 00:00:32.910
vended credentials.

16
00:00:34.720 --> 00:00:37.130
Our tables live on OCI Object Storage,

17
00:00:37.540 --> 00:00:39.840
it speaks S3, but there's no STS

18
00:00:39.860 --> 00:00:41.853
behind it, so Polaris has nothing to

19
00:00:41.873 --> 00:00:42.250
vend.

20
00:00:42.660 --> 00:00:44.690
Getting ClickHouse to read took three errors,

21
00:00:45.040 --> 00:00:45.570
a 403,

22
00:00:46.120 --> 00:00:46.590
a 400,

23
00:00:47.100 --> 00:00:47.910
then one setting.

24
00:00:48.880 --> 00:00:50.450
I thought one privilege was the fix,

25
00:00:50.780 --> 00:00:53.120
it wasn't, this lab shows why, we

26
00:00:53.140 --> 00:00:54.560
take a grant away and see what

27
00:00:54.580 --> 00:00:56.490
still reads, you can run it yourself.

28
00:00:57.940 --> 00:00:59.767
First, how Polaris decides.

29
00:00:59.787 --> 00:01:01.880
You never grant a privilege to a

30
00:01:01.900 --> 00:01:02.790
principal directly.

31
00:01:03.800 --> 00:01:06.200
ch_reader is a principal, it belongs to

32
00:01:06.220 --> 00:01:08.700
a principal role ch_role, that holds a

33
00:01:08.720 --> 00:01:11.420
catalog role, the reader_all role, only the

34
00:01:11.440 --> 00:01:13.090
catalog role carries privileges.

35
00:01:14.180 --> 00:01:15.270
Seven read privileges,

36
00:01:15.860 --> 00:01:18.010
the one that matters today is TABLE_READ_DATA.

37
00:01:19.380 --> 00:01:21.160
ClickHouse can load a table from Polaris

38
00:01:21.180 --> 00:01:22.170
in two ways,

39
00:01:22.880 --> 00:01:25.240
a plain loadTable, which only needs metadata

40
00:01:25.260 --> 00:01:25.910
privileges,

41
00:01:26.420 --> 00:01:28.610
or a load table with read delegation,

42
00:01:29.240 --> 00:01:32.130
that's the vended credentials, it needs TABLE_READ_DATA,

43
00:01:32.500 --> 00:01:34.370
and ClickHouse asks for it by default.

44
00:01:35.140 --> 00:01:36.600
With the grant in place, both return

45
00:01:36.620 --> 00:01:39.050
200 and ClickHouse reads the rows.

46
00:01:40.360 --> 00:01:43.370
Now revoke TABLE_READ_DATA from the reader_all role,

47
00:01:44.040 --> 00:01:46.160
the plain load still works, the delegated

48
00:01:46.180 --> 00:01:47.730
one is now a 403.

49
00:01:49.620 --> 00:01:52.240
And ClickHouse, it still lists the table,

50
00:01:52.260 --> 00:01:54.830
then count says the table doesn't exist.

51
00:01:56.900 --> 00:01:59.280
That's the 403, hidden, turn on debug

52
00:01:59.300 --> 00:02:01.740
logs, and Polaris' real answer shows up,

53
00:02:01.760 --> 00:02:03.870
including which roles it actually resolved.

54
00:02:06.180 --> 00:02:08.560
Admin logins fail the same way, this

55
00:02:08.580 --> 00:02:10.560
lab had added manage content to catalog

56
00:02:10.580 --> 00:02:12.760
admin, take it off, and you're back

57
00:02:12.780 --> 00:02:15.420
to what Polaris creates, manage access, and

58
00:02:15.440 --> 00:02:17.230
manage metadata, nothing more.

59
00:02:18.060 --> 00:02:21.360
Neither includes TABLE_READ_DATA, so root gets the

60
00:02:21.380 --> 00:02:22.890
same 403 from Polaris.

61
00:02:25.300 --> 00:02:27.500
Now tell ClickHouse not to ask for

62
00:02:27.520 --> 00:02:28.110
vended credentials,

63
00:02:28.760 --> 00:02:29.470
vended credentials,

64
00:02:30.240 --> 00:02:30.430
false.

65
00:02:31.560 --> 00:02:33.880
ch_reader still without the grant reads the

66
00:02:33.900 --> 00:02:34.250
rows.

67
00:02:35.580 --> 00:02:38.110
And so does root, with vending off,

68
00:02:38.320 --> 00:02:40.390
Polaris never decided who reads the files,

69
00:02:40.860 --> 00:02:43.374
the storage key does, you'll see it

70
00:02:43.394 --> 00:02:45.522
in the DDL in a moment.

71
00:02:45.542 --> 00:02:48.028
On OCI there's no STS, so Polaris

72
00:02:48.048 --> 00:02:49.630
has nothing to vend.

73
00:02:49.940 --> 00:02:51.640
With the grant fixed, ClickHouse got a

74
00:02:51.660 --> 00:02:52.130
400.

75
00:02:53.240 --> 00:02:54.270
Authorization passed,

76
00:02:54.760 --> 00:02:55.350
vending failed,

77
00:02:55.820 --> 00:02:57.880
this lab answers that call differently, so

78
00:02:57.900 --> 00:02:59.330
this one is from OCI.

79
00:03:01.100 --> 00:03:03.110
This is the DDL that just worked,

80
00:03:03.520 --> 00:03:06.250
DataLakeCatalog, not the Iceberg table function.

81
00:03:07.040 --> 00:03:08.990
The two keys are static and read-only,

82
00:03:09.360 --> 00:03:11.520
catalog credential is the reader's client ID

83
00:03:11.540 --> 00:03:14.330
and secret, vended credentials is false.

84
00:03:14.780 --> 00:03:16.960
On OCI, only the token issuer, the

85
00:03:16.980 --> 00:03:19.070
scope and the warehouse scheme change.

86
00:03:21.600 --> 00:03:24.520
Before touching ClickHouse, check authorization with two

87
00:03:24.540 --> 00:03:25.770
curls as the reader.

88
00:03:26.420 --> 00:03:28.240
Plain is what ClickHouse does with vending

89
00:03:28.260 --> 00:03:30.800
off, delegated is the default, and it's

90
00:03:30.820 --> 00:03:33.130
403 because the grant is still revoked.

91
00:03:33.680 --> 00:03:35.160
That's the unknown table you saw in

92
00:03:35.180 --> 00:03:35.810
ClickHouse.

93
00:03:37.920 --> 00:03:39.950
When you hit an error, map it,

94
00:03:40.160 --> 00:03:42.500
unknown table after SHOW TABLES works, a

95
00:03:42.520 --> 00:03:43.270
hidden 403,

96
00:03:43.860 --> 00:03:46.380
a 400, nothing to vend, Code 117

97
00:03:46.400 --> 00:03:49.160
on a manifest, compaction, or a bigger

98
00:03:49.180 --> 00:03:50.850
node, not a grant problem.

99
00:03:52.400 --> 00:03:55.668
Keep it small, one catalog role, one

100
00:03:55.688 --> 00:03:58.280
principal role, one principal, one read-only key

101
00:03:58.300 --> 00:03:59.370
scoped to the warehouse.

102
00:03:59.940 --> 00:04:01.250
The discipline is the design.

103
00:04:03.080 --> 00:04:05.880
Grant TABLE_READ_DATA back, you'll need it the

104
00:04:05.900 --> 00:04:06.930
day the store can vend.

105
00:04:07.240 --> 00:04:08.710
the lab goes back as it was,

106
00:04:08.920 --> 00:04:10.340
the full write-up and the lab are

107
00:04:10.360 --> 00:04:10.990
linked below.

